3. Simulate a boot failure by editing the /etc/fstab file and adding a fake mount entry, then reboot your VM and document the error message that appears during boot.<br><br><em><strong>Constraint:</strong> Restore your original /etc/fstab after testing to avoid permanent boot issues.</em>
==>cp /etc/fstab /etc/fstab.bak
echo "/dev/doesnotexist /mnt/fake xfs defaults 0 0" >> /etc/fstab
reboot
      Failed to mount /mnt/fake.
      Dependency failed for Local File Systems.
      You are in emergency mode...
RESTORE:
cp /etc/fstab.bak /etc/fstab
systemctl daemon-reload
reboot


